# The two encodings the text patterns are written in, as 32-bit words.
#
# A piece is a tree written in prefix order: a node's kind, its operands, then its children. The pieces a program
# builds (`digit`, `capture(...)`, `TextPattern.of([...])`) are this tree, in every language: RazorForge and Suflae
# build the same words and hand them to the same compiler through Ingrid.
#
#   NODE_LITERAL n u1 .. un             the units in a row (code points of a text, or bytes)
#   NODE_RANGES negated n lo1 hi1 ..    one unit in one of the ranges (or in none of them when negated is 1)
#   NODE_SEQUENCE n child1 .. childn    the children one after another
#   NODE_EITHER_LONGER n child1 ..      one of the children: the one that matches the longest text there
#   NODE_EITHER_SHORTER n child1 ..     one of the children: the one that matches the shortest text there
#   NODE_REPEAT min max child           the child min to max times (max REPEAT_UNBOUNDED for no limit), greedy
#   NODE_CAPTURE n c1 .. cn child       the child, its text kept under the name c1 .. cn (code points)
#   NODE_ANCHOR kind                    a place, matching no text (ANCHOR_START_OF_TEXT ..)
#   NODE_IGNORE_CASE child              the child, with each letter matching in either case
#   NODE_CLASS id negated               a named class (CLASS_DIGIT ..), or every unit outside it
#
# A program is what the compiler makes of a pattern's tree: a header of HEADER_WORDS words, the instructions (three
# words each: operation, a, b), the class ranges, the either table and the capture names. The engine (Engine.te)
# runs it over text or bytes.

module Text/Patterns

### A piece node: units in a row.
preset NODE_LITERAL: U32 = 1
### A piece node: one unit in (or outside) a list of ranges.
preset NODE_RANGES: U32 = 2
### A piece node: children one after another.
preset NODE_SEQUENCE: U32 = 3
### A piece node: the child that matches the longest text.
preset NODE_EITHER_LONGER: U32 = 4
### A piece node: the child that matches the shortest text.
preset NODE_EITHER_SHORTER: U32 = 5
### A piece node: the child repeated.
preset NODE_REPEAT: U32 = 6
### A piece node: the child's text kept under a name.
preset NODE_CAPTURE: U32 = 7
### A piece node: a place that matches no text.
preset NODE_ANCHOR: U32 = 8
### A piece node: the child matched without regard to case.
preset NODE_IGNORE_CASE: U32 = 9
### A piece node: one unit of a named class.
preset NODE_CLASS: U32 = 10

### The largest count a repetition takes, written for "no limit".
preset REPEAT_UNBOUNDED: U32 = 4294967295

### The beginning of the text.
preset ANCHOR_START_OF_TEXT: U32 = 0
### The end of the text.
preset ANCHOR_END_OF_TEXT: U32 = 1
### The beginning of the text or the place after a line feed.
preset ANCHOR_START_OF_LINE: U32 = 2
### The end of the text or the place before a line feed.
preset ANCHOR_END_OF_LINE: U32 = 3
### A place between a word character and a character that isn't one (the ends of the text count as the second).
preset ANCHOR_WORD_BOUNDARY: U32 = 4
### A place that isn't a word boundary.
preset ANCHOR_NOT_WORD_BOUNDARY: U32 = 5

### The ASCII digits 0 to 9.
preset CLASS_DIGIT: U32 = 0
### The ASCII letters a to z and A to Z.
preset CLASS_LETTER: U32 = 1
### The ASCII whitespace: space, tab, line feed, vertical tab, form feed, carriage return.
preset CLASS_SPACE: U32 = 2
### The ASCII word characters: letters, digits and the underscore.
preset CLASS_WORD_CHAR: U32 = 3
### Any character, or any byte in a bytes pattern.
preset CLASS_ANY: U32 = 4
### The Unicode decimal digits (Nd).
preset CLASS_UNICODE_DIGIT: U32 = 5
### The Unicode letters (L).
preset CLASS_UNICODE_LETTER: U32 = 6
### The Unicode whitespace (White_Space).
preset CLASS_UNICODE_SPACE: U32 = 7
### The Unicode word characters: letters, marks, decimal digits and connector punctuation.
preset CLASS_UNICODE_WORD_CHAR: U32 = 8

### A program over text: its units are code points.
preset MODE_TEXT: U32 = 0
### A program over bytes: its units are bytes.
preset MODE_BYTES: U32 = 1

### The first word of every program.
preset PROGRAM_MAGIC: U32 = 0x50544E31
### The number of header words before the first instruction.
preset HEADER_WORDS: U64 = 16
### The header word that holds the mode.
preset HEADER_MODE: U64 = 1
### The header word that holds the number of instructions.
preset HEADER_INSTRUCTIONS: U64 = 2
### The header word that holds the number of named captures.
preset HEADER_GROUPS: U64 = 3
### The header word that holds where the class ranges start.
preset HEADER_RANGES: U64 = 4
### The header word that holds where the either table starts.
preset HEADER_EITHERS: U64 = 5
### The header word that holds where the capture names start.
preset HEADER_NAMES: U64 = 6
### The header word that holds the program's length in words.
preset HEADER_LENGTH: U64 = 7

### An instruction: match one unit equal to a.
preset OP_UNIT: U32 = 1
### An instruction: match one unit in the b ranges that start at word a.
preset OP_CLASS: U32 = 2
### An instruction: go on at a, and at b when that fails.
preset OP_SPLIT: U32 = 3
### An instruction: go on at a.
preset OP_JUMP: U32 = 4
### An instruction: keep the position in capture slot a.
preset OP_SAVE: U32 = 5
### An instruction: go on only where the anchor a holds.
preset OP_ASSERT: U32 = 6
### An instruction: one of the alternatives in the either entry at word a, chosen by length (b 0 longer, 1 shorter).
preset OP_EITHER: U32 = 7
### An instruction: the end of an alternative, going on at a.
preset OP_END_ALT: U32 = 8
### An instruction: a match ends here.
preset OP_MATCH: U32 = 9

### The most instructions a program may have.
preset MAX_INSTRUCTIONS: U64 = 1000000

### The position written for a capture that took no part in a match.
preset NO_POSITION: U64 = 18446744073709551615
